      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The scandal led to the Civil Rights of Institutionalized Persons Act of 1980, protecting people with disabilities nationwide.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Willowbrook_State_School",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Willowbrook State School operated from 1947 until 1987, once the largest state‑run institution for mental disabilities in the U.S.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21,
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Willowbrook_State_School",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "After closure, part of the campus became the College of Staten Island’s campus, bringing higher education to the area.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Willowbrook_State_School",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "In 1983, New York announced plans to close Willowbrook, renaming it the Staten Island Developmental Center in 1974.",
